  "term": "pethidine",
  "definition": "Pethidine is a narcotic pain-relieving drug used for moderate to severe pain, including pain after surgery and during labor. With prolonged use, it can cause morphine-type dependence, and its withdrawal symptoms tend to begin sooner than morphine’s and last for a shorter time.",
